<title>USA: Louisville feeder cattle not well tested - USDA.</title>
<headline>Louisville feeder cattle not well tested - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>LOUISVILLE 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers were not well tested last week, compared to last Monday's close, USDA said. However, feeder steers were $1.00 to $3.00 higher and heifers firm to $2.00 higher than before the Holiday break.</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - Medium and Large 1 600-700 lbs 56.00-60.50; 700-800 lbs few 54.00-62.50; 800-900 lbs few 57.00-61.50; 900-950 lbs few 55.00-60.25. Small 1 500-600 lbs 42.50- 50.00. Holstein Large 2 Couple 617 lbs 37.00; 1000-1250 lbs 42.00-42.50.</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers - Medium and Large 1 600-700 lbs 49.00-54.00; 700-800 lbs 48.50-55.00. Small 1 400-500 lbs 36.00-42.00. Medium and Large 2 600-700 lbs 40.00-46.00. Medium and Large 2 500-650 lbs 33.00-41.00. Cattle and Calves Receipts - 3,200</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
